The PlayStation(R)Vita build's dtrace.c (contrib/sce-dtrace-cddl-2015.01, as Sony published it) with
one change of ours, not Sony's: dtrace_dof_copyin is noinline. Sony's GCC keeps it whole in every
build (3.6x 0x81008180, 4.00 0x81009da8; called by dtrace_ioctl and dtrace_ioctl_helper), ours
inlines it into both callers once ASSERT is compiled out. The change stays on its line, so the
debug records keep Sony's line numbers.

--- a/dtrace/cddl/dtrace.c
+++ b/dtrace/cddl/dtrace.c
@@ -14795,7 +14795,7 @@
 	return (dof);
 }
 
-static dof_hdr_t *
+static __attribute__((noinline)) dof_hdr_t *
 #if !defined(__APPLE__)
 dtrace_dof_copyin(uintptr_t uarg, int *errp)
 #else
